{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal by reason of substandard layout, unsatisfactory access to private amenity space for the upper floor flat and lack of demonstration of functionality of each habitable room, represents over-intensification and over-development of the site that would result in sub-standard living conditions and environment, to the detriment of the amenities of future occupiers.  The proposal would therefore be contrary to, in particular, polices H11.1 and D12.3 of the Merton Local Plan 2024, Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and the Technical Housing Standards - Nationally Described Space Standard.",
    "Reason : 2 - The development has failed to provide sufficient secure, integrated, convenient and accessible cycle parking facilities, contrary to policy T16.2 of  Merton's Local Plan 2024 and T5 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "Reason : 3 - In the absence of adequate refuse and recycling storage facilities for the development, the applicant has not demonstrated that the scheme would safeguard the free flow of traffic in the locality to the detriment of highway and pedestrian safety and safeguard the visual amenity  of the area.  The scheme is contrary to, in particular, Policies D4, SI 7 & SI 8 of the London Plan 2021,  Merton Local Plan 2024 policy D12.2, D12.3 and W14.4.",
    "Reason : 4 - The applicant has failed to provide a satisfactory soft-landscaping scheme or any biodiversity measures, thereby failing to comply the objectives set out in G5 of the London Plan 2021",
    "Reason : 5 - In the absence of an Air Quality Neutral Statement, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the development would be at minimum air quality neutral, not worsening local air quality thereby failing to comply with policy SI1 of the London Plan 2021",
    "Reason : 6 - By reason of the scheme failing to achieve Zero Carbon and the absence of a legal agreement to secure the required carbon offset fund the scheme fails to provide a sustainable and energy efficient scheme contrary to the aims and objectives of, in particular, policy CC2.2 of Merton Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 7 - In the absence of a legal agreement to secure an appropriate contribution towards offsite affordable housing or a satisfactory financial viability assessment to justify the lack of, the scheme fails to address the recognised housing need and will be contrary to, in particular, Policy H11.1 of Merton's Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 8 - In the absence of a satisfactory flood risk assessment incorporating drainage strategy the scheme is considered to increase risk of flooding in the locality contrary to the aims and objections of, in particular, London Plan policy SI 13, Merton Local Plan 2024 Policy O15.9.",
    "Reason : 9 - In the absence of a noise impact assessment detailing any necessary mitigation measures required with the installation of the Heat Pump, the scheme is considered to harm the residential amenity of nearby occupants contrary to, in particular, Policy P15.10 of Merton Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 10 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe application was not considered to comply with the provisions of the Development Plan and NPPF as submitted, and would have required substantial changes such that a new application would be required. \r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n"
  ],
